+# Unit45 — Backend-owned FFSX/Plotly import (pending Actions)
+
+## Policy, Source audit and missed translation guard
+
+Continue development-policy.md v0.2.6 read fully (1228 lines) and AGENT.md numeric paired patch/lineage/single authority rules. Source remains highest authority; no policy changes, local application/test/build/checker or optional TLC execution. Source45 application/public_api/graphs.py importSelectedGraphFile forwards explicit slot/file only, requires Backend parsing/candidate/one commit, gates official graphs.readData success read. Source45 backend/assets_files.py applyFfsxSlot resolves the current target, maps only actual real CSV references into new project ids/paths, preserves noneditable conversion views and package caption, and validates the whole candidate before caller commit. Existing common transaction requires source replacement retry. The Source does not restrict target to preexisting graph content; the public raw/slot router also delegates package files for a captured visible slot.
+
+Pseudocode23 backend/project_efsm.pcal had ResolveCurrentVisibleGraphSlot in SLOT_CHART_IMPORTED despite these Source/public contracts. Prior whole translation review missed this extra precondition by not checking image-content target delegation against the branch. Correct pseudocode first to ResolveCurrentVisibleSlot, preserving Source45 meaning rather than altering Source to justify a lower restriction. Pseudocode24 directly derives the unchanged Source45 fingerprint. No new higher-level requirement, no rewritten ownership hierarchy or optional model gate.
+
+## Direct implementation and bounded checklist
+
+Code96 receives only explicit slot id plus detached raw file bytes; existing synchronous Project EFSM remains synchronous. Application may await pure copied byte preparation, not parse/compute persistent charts/candidates. The command parses/validates bytes using existing package parser/private copied-byte entry or Plotly parser, resolves current visible target, and creates one private candidate preserving canonical content. Real package CSV ids are unique/remapped once per referenced local id with current project id and current VFS unique path; conversion rows/imported figures are not rewritten as fake CSV. Replaces only the target's owned chart/reference/content type and package caption, keeps image settings/extensions and unrelated selection/assets, validates then compares source reference/retries whole calculation before one commit. Actual chart/slot/CSV/path/owners and matching chart-specific selectedIndexHint drive common reconciliation. Public wrapper returns official copied chart on commit, propagates original errors and never rolls back a late failure. Existing aggregate renderer remains not a claimed supplied-dashboard closure. Removed obsolete importSlotFile Application parser/transaction; ffsxReadSlot retains a pure file-byte convenience wrapper around the same private parser for read-only callers/tests.
+
+- Case122: actual exported FFSX, repeated objects share one new real CSV, raw minimal command payload, one commit/current ids/actual facts, image target becomes graph while custom settings/canonical extension survive, unrelated graph/CSV selection stays.
+- Case123: malformed input/invalid target/validation failure unchanged, exact original errors, noncommit skips success reads, replacement during validation recalculates new chart id and preserves newer metadata, late official read failure does not undo commit.
+- Case124: actual Plotly bytes -> noneditable conversion chart -> real FFSX roundtrip to another slot; imported graph/rows preserved and no fake CSV created. Prior121 cases retain broader actual import/export/candidate checks.
+
+## Lineage, pending evidence and limits
+
+Source45 unchanged e68cab90bdfa0a98acf704d6c84374d02d5c818a0afd018bf1af714b27fdc8a7; pseudocode24 fcc1dab67abc9ab37a6ef42f187726555507cee32adeee585aa25abc2183c9b4; code96 52448be81eafaa1f6d06551fc8d7ca36cade75f6e25b29a3f6a597ca6157a18a remains stale. Digests calculated from staged Git path/blob identities, not local checker execution; canonical Actions confirmation pending. Exact-SHA124 inline+124 split/repeat/build/cumulative development-layer/fidelity PENDING. Static fidelity gate is not semantic proof. Whole common commit/other mutation owners, schema/serializer, raster/current-snapshot resources, supplied dashboard and timing/lifecycle requirements still open. No whole-goal closure from bounded tests or manifest. No explicit quota/auth/service blocker observed.
